Yes. The part of the program that depends on the model follows the usage shown in the official example. The model is loaded from the supplied weights file and then wrapped in a predictor. Each cell is offered as a single box and the first mask that is returned is taken. That mask is reduced to the outline of its largest portion and any part of it that lies on top of a mask already accepted is taken away. The result is a single unbroken figure for each cell. Everything else in the file has been as far as possible checked against the sample material supplied. Introducing the missing packages into this container would not have the effect of altering any of that.

